    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Analysis of the grid event reveals a sequence of documented failures: a recorded operational disruption at Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2, part of a documented cluster of equipment failures since May began, led to a quantified loss of over 950 megawatts. This measurable deficit, compounded by a verifiable demand-supply squeeze from seasonal heat, triggered the activation of a high-level grid emergency protocol in the Visayas, resulting in an increased probability of managed outages.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
        "fragments": [
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "why-2",
          "result-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The grid authority's decision-making process is evidenced by its response to a measurable deficit in the system. Following a generation unit failure and sustained generation unavailability, officials ordered a load management directive as a technical response to avert line failure, acting on grid stability calculations. This preventive action, grounded in infrastructure protection data, aimed to prevent cascading failure from overloading a high-voltage transmission line.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
